2264
01:31:28,650 --> 01:31:31,353
Fortunately for you, and for us.

2265
01:31:31,387 --> 01:31:32,455
- I just talked to Berringer.

2266
01:31:32,488 --> 01:31:33,822
He wants to see it immediately.

2267
01:31:33,857 --> 01:31:35,725
- Good, I'm glad he does.

2268
01:31:35,758 --> 01:31:37,660
The sooner we get
rid of it, the better

2269
01:31:37,693 --> 01:31:38,895
Oh, Marta, come on in.

2270
01:31:40,262 --> 01:31:41,063
- Is it all right?

2271
01:31:41,097 --> 01:31:42,332
- For a little while.

2272
01:31:42,365 --> 01:31:43,198
I think it'll do him
more good than harm.

2273
01:31:43,232 --> 01:31:44,033
Excuse me.

2274
01:31:44,067 --> 01:31:45,333
- [Tom] I think so too.

2275
01:31:45,367 --> 01:31:47,270
- Are you sure you
got that thing fixed

2276
01:31:47,303 --> 01:31:48,503
so it won't ever get away again?

2277
01:31:48,537 --> 01:31:49,805
- Don't worry about it, Sheriff.

2278
01:31:49,838 --> 01:31:51,640
It's in a metal box,
and it's locked,

2279
01:31:51,673 --> 01:31:53,275
and in about two minutes
it's gonna be on an airplane,

2280
01:31:53,308 --> 01:31:54,877
and no one will
ever see it again.

2281
01:31:54,910 --> 01:31:57,045
- [Tom] Unless the weather
starts getting rough.

2282
01:31:57,078 --> 01:31:59,582
- [Crow] Well, I'm on my
way for a three hour tour.

2283
01:32:01,850 --> 01:32:03,118
- Come on, tell me,

2284
01:32:04,287 --> 01:32:05,287
did you mean what
you said last night,

2285
01:32:05,320 --> 01:32:06,822
about staying here?

2286
01:32:06,855 --> 01:32:07,857
- [Tom] Yes, I intend not to.

2287
01:32:07,890 --> 01:32:10,092
- I don't play games.

2288
01:32:10,125 --> 01:32:11,293
Too weak.

2289
01:32:11,327 --> 01:32:13,128
- How can I help myself?

2290
01:32:13,162 --> 01:32:15,732
You know women can't
resist weak men.

2291
01:32:15,765 --> 01:32:17,400
- Then you're gonna stay?

2292
01:32:17,433 --> 01:32:19,802
- [Tom] Or the rich
taste of smores.

2293
01:32:19,835 --> 01:32:21,937
- Just wait til I
get out of this bed.

2294
01:32:21,970 --> 01:32:22,805
Just you.

2295
01:32:24,273 --> 01:32:27,075
- [Tom] And me,
and my extra arm.

2296
01:32:33,682 --> 01:32:36,018
- [Crow] Oh no,
not these two guys.

2297
01:32:36,052 --> 01:32:36,952
- [Joel] Man, they
couldn't even work

2298
01:32:36,985 --> 01:32:39,522
for Domino's pizza delivery.

2299
01:32:39,555 --> 01:32:41,523
- [Tom] About time
for a tall cool one.

2300
01:32:42,725 --> 01:32:44,493
A couple of road sodas.

2301
01:32:46,495 --> 01:32:48,297
- Wonder what all the
secrecy's about this time.

2302
01:32:48,330 --> 01:32:49,832
- There you go, sticking
your nose into something

2303
01:32:49,865 --> 01:32:51,333
that's none of your business.

2304
01:32:51,367 --> 01:32:52,968
All we're supposed to do is
deliver it to the airport.

2305
01:32:53,002 --> 01:32:55,570
- Yeah, but those people
inside got me curious.

2306
01:32:55,605 --> 01:32:56,738
You know that fella
from Washington,

2307
01:32:56,772 --> 01:32:58,040
the way he kept looking at it,

2308
01:32:58,073 --> 01:33:00,008
asking me if I was
sure it was locked.

2309
01:33:02,645 --> 01:33:04,347
I'd give anything to
take a look inside.

2310
01:33:04,380 --> 01:33:06,182
- Not me, I don't
care what's in it.

2311
01:33:06,215 --> 01:33:07,317
Come on, let's get moving.

2312
01:33:07,350 --> 01:33:08,883
- That's your
trouble. No curiosity.

2313
01:33:08,917 --> 01:33:11,053
You will never get any
place without curiosity.

2314
01:33:11,087 --> 01:33:12,722
You gotta find out about things.

2315
01:33:12,755 --> 01:33:15,457
- Yeah, well I like it that way.

2316
01:33:15,490 --> 01:33:17,092
- What harm would it
do to take a look?

2317
01:33:17,125 --> 01:33:18,660
I've got the key.

2318
01:33:18,693 --> 01:33:20,462
- It might be dangerous.

2319
01:33:20,495 --> 01:33:22,063
- What do you think, it's alive?

2320
01:33:22,097 --> 01:33:24,067
You don't see any
holes in the box.

2321
01:33:24,100 --> 01:33:25,467
You think it'll bite
you or something?

2322
01:33:25,500 --> 01:33:27,002
- [Tom] Way to go, Mr. Logic.

2323
01:33:27,035 --> 01:33:28,537
- Always talking me into doing
something I don't want to do.

2324
01:33:28,570 --> 01:33:30,640
- Have I ever steered you wrong?

2325
01:33:30,673 --> 01:33:32,240
- [Tom] Well, there's
that whole beer,

2326
01:33:32,273 --> 01:33:34,510
dead body thing, yeah.

2327
01:33:34,543 --> 01:33:35,745
- [Crow] No, don't do it guys.

2328
01:33:35,778 --> 01:33:37,245
- [Tom] We better
get out of here.

2329
01:33:38,313 --> 01:33:39,215
Here, come on.
- [Joel] Don't do it!

2330
01:33:39,248 --> 01:33:39,915
- [Tom] Let's go, you guys.

2331
01:33:39,948 --> 01:33:41,150
(Crow screaming)

2332
01:33:41,183 --> 01:33:43,385
- [Crow] Next time
use Federal Express.

2333
01:33:43,418 --> 01:33:44,687
Or maybe hand delivery.

2334
01:33:46,722 --> 01:33:49,025
(dramatic music)

2335
01:33:49,058 --> 01:33:50,092
♪ Mockingbird ♪

2336
01:33:50,125 --> 01:33:51,693
♪ Bird's the word ♪

2337
01:33:51,727 --> 01:33:52,862
♪ Bird, bird's the word ♪

2338
01:33:52,895 --> 01:33:55,832
(mysterious music)

2339
01:34:03,472 --> 01:34:05,742
- Okay, you guys, that's
the end of the movie.

2340
01:34:05,775 --> 01:34:06,975
We made it.

2341
01:34:07,008 --> 01:34:10,312
And this is time for
the Ram Chip episode,

2342
01:34:10,345 --> 01:34:12,047
where you say a good
thing about the film,

2343
01:34:12,080 --> 01:34:14,283
and a bad thing,
you get a ram chip.

2344
01:34:14,317 --> 01:34:15,785
Ready, go ahead Crow.

2345
01:34:16,918 --> 01:34:18,220
- Well, let's see.

2346
01:34:18,253 --> 01:34:19,722
The good thing was
those cats showed us

2347
01:34:19,755 --> 01:34:24,327
a new definition for
finger food. (laughing)

2348
01:34:24,360 --> 01:34:25,795
- And the bad thing?

2349
01:34:25,828 --> 01:34:28,730
- Bad thing was, well,
never trust a deliveryman.

2350
01:34:28,763 --> 01:34:29,565
- Okay, here's your ram chip.

2351
01:34:29,598 --> 01:34:30,632
There you go.

2352
01:34:30,665 --> 01:34:32,702
Now, Tom Servo.

2353
01:34:32,735 --> 01:34:35,570
- Okay, the good thing was
there was a Swedish babe

2354
01:34:35,603 --> 01:34:37,305
in the film, who
didn't get killed.

2355
01:34:37,338 --> 01:34:38,840
- Yeah, and the bad thing.

2356
01:34:38,873 --> 01:34:41,110
- She didn't spend the time
on her makeup that it deserved

2357
01:34:41,143 --> 01:34:42,277
as the film went on.

2358
01:34:42,310 --> 01:34:43,645
- Okay, here's
your ram chip, pal.

2359
01:34:43,678 --> 01:34:44,480
There you go.

2360
01:34:44,513 --> 01:34:45,848
All right.

2361
01:34:45,882 --> 01:34:47,248
Well, we want to thank
everybody who's been writing in,

2362
01:34:47,282 --> 01:34:48,817
and I want to thank
the mad scientists

2363
01:34:48,850 --> 01:34:51,287
for faxing the
letters back up to me.

2364
01:34:51,320 --> 01:34:55,457
But anyway, this one's from
Ricky Fowls, and he says,

2365
01:34:55,490 --> 01:34:57,993
he wrote some letters, and
this one's to you, Crow.

2366
01:34:58,027 --> 01:34:59,862
He goes, "Dear Crow.

2367
01:34:59,895 --> 01:35:01,563
"I really like you.

2368
01:35:01,597 --> 01:35:03,898
"I laugh when you make a joke."

2369
01:35:03,932 --> 01:35:05,033
So that's a good thing, right?

2370
01:35:05,067 --> 01:35:06,168
- Have I made one yet?

2371
01:35:06,202 --> 01:35:07,437
- Yeah.

2372
01:35:07,470 --> 01:35:09,838
"And I hope I can
see you someday."

2373
01:35:10,773 --> 01:35:12,207
- Take a look, kid.

2374
01:35:12,240 --> 01:35:16,412
"And Joel, someday I would
like you to take apart Servo."

2375
01:35:16,445 --> 01:35:17,613
- Hey, can I help?

2376
01:35:17,647 --> 01:35:21,083
- "And I like Gypsy,
because he looks cool."

2377
01:35:21,117 --> 01:35:22,752
Gypsy's a she, by the way.

2378
01:35:24,187 --> 01:35:26,988
That's from Ricky Fowls, and
he also did some drawings.

2379
01:35:27,022 --> 01:35:28,890
We got those in still
store, don't we Cambot?

2380
01:35:28,923 --> 01:35:30,092
Okay, let's take a look at that.

2381
01:35:30,125 --> 01:35:32,428
We got one of Crow,

2382
01:35:32,462 --> 01:35:34,597
and then it says,
"Look on back."

2383
01:35:34,630 --> 01:35:35,730
And you turn it around,

2384
01:35:35,765 --> 01:35:37,800
and we got a Tom Servo there.

2385
01:35:37,833 --> 01:35:39,067
(robots gushing)
See, isn't that neat?

2386
01:35:39,102 --> 01:35:41,737
And then, on the next
one, it says, "Gypsy".

2387
01:35:41,770 --> 01:35:42,972
It's like this.

2388
01:35:43,005 --> 01:35:44,507
And then it says,
"Look on back."

2389
01:35:44,540 --> 01:35:45,942
And it's got Joel.

2390
01:35:45,975 --> 01:35:48,143
Right there, see I got a little
light bulb above my head.

2391
01:35:48,177 --> 01:35:50,112
'Cause I had a bright idea.

2392
01:35:50,145 --> 01:35:52,347
All right, well, read
the address, Crow.

2393
01:35:52,380 --> 01:35:53,582
Keep the cards and
letters coming in.

2394
01:35:53,615 --> 01:35:54,450
- Can I do it, buddy?

2395
01:35:54,483 --> 01:35:55,383
- Servo, read it.

2396
01:35:55,417 --> 01:35:57,185
- Tom Servo, read the letter.

2397
01:35:57,218 --> 01:35:58,553
- All right, send your letters

2398
01:35:58,587 --> 01:36:00,488
to the Mystery Science
Theater Fan Club.

2399
01:36:00,522 --> 01:36:02,592
P.O. Box 5325.

2400
01:36:02,625 --> 01:36:05,560
Hopkins, Minnesota, 55343.

2401
01:36:05,593 --> 01:36:07,530
Send them now.

2402
01:36:07,563 --> 01:36:08,930
- Thanks a lot for watching.

2403
01:36:08,963 --> 01:36:11,500
Scientists, I hope you're happy.

2404
01:36:11,533 --> 01:36:12,835
- Yeah, yeah, I'm happy.

2405
01:36:12,868 --> 01:36:14,170
Are you happy, Clyde?

2406
01:36:14,203 --> 01:36:15,170
(Clyde grunting)

2407
01:36:15,203 --> 01:36:17,172
Tell 'em, are you happy?

2408
01:36:17,205 --> 01:36:18,340
Tell 'em.

2409
01:36:18,373 --> 01:36:21,077
- Got to reach console.

2410
01:36:21,110 --> 01:36:23,412
Got to end experiment.
